 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 513223,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Solve the system by graphing:\n<br>\n<span data-math=\"\\left\\{ {\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}} {x + y \\leq 2} \\\\  {y \\geq \\frac{2}{3}x - 1} \\end{array}} \\right.\">\\left\\{ {\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}} {x + y \\leq 2} \\\\  {y \\geq \\frac{2}{3}x - 1} \\end{array}} \\right.</span>\n\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"x + y \\le 2\"></span></p>\n<p>Graph the first line as a solid line using intercepts: <span data-math=\"\\left( {2,0} \\right)\"></span>and <span data-math=\"\\left( {0,2} \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Test (0, 0).</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"0 + 0 \\le 2\"></span></td>\n<td>This is true. Shade lightly the side where (0, 0) is located.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"y \\ge \\frac{2}{3}x - 1\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Graph the second line as a solid line using the intercept <span data-math=\"\\left( {0, - 1} \\right)\"></span> and the slope of <span data-math=\"\\frac{2}{3}\"></span>.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Test (0, 0).</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"0 \\ge \\frac{2}{3}\\left( 0 \\right) - 1\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"0 \\ge  - 1\"></span></td>\n<td>This is also true. Shade lightly the side where (0, 0) is located.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The solution is the region shaded by both graphs.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The solution is the darkest shaded region.<br>\n<img src=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBcllLIiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--bfc47448308d211ba57eab36fa900c3ffe7b01fd/CS_Figure_05_10_005.jpg\" alt=\"Two lines are plotted on a coordinate plane. The horizontal and vertical axes range from negative 10 to 10, in increments of 1. The first line passes through the points, (negative 7, 9), (0, 2), (2, 0), and (9, negative 7). The region below the line is shaded in dark blue. The second line passes through the points, (negative 9, negative 7), (0, negative 1), and (9, 5). The region above the line is shaded in light blue. The two lines intersect approximately at (1.8, 0.3). The region to the left of the intersection point and within the lines is shaded in gray.\">"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
